{
  "about": "Familiar dimensionless groups, each stored as formulas over quantities with explicit reference quantities, never as a name alone (spec section 10). A group matches a calculated group when one of its forms gives the same exponent for each supplied variable through a one-to-one match of quantities. phase, kind and role narrow a term: phase fluid or solid; kind parameter (the default, which also matches a constant), field, coordinate or any. A recognized name is a proposed interpretation until the researcher confirms it. Order is the preference order for a familiar basis.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "id": "Nu",
      "tex": "Nu",
      "label": "Nu",
      "name": "Nusselt number",
      "def": "Nu=\\frac{hL}{k_f}",
      "plain": "Nu = hL/k_f",
      "forms": [
        [
          {
            "q": "heat-transfer-coefficient",
            "e": 1
          },
          {
            "q": "length",
            "e": 1
          },
          {
            "q": "thermal-conductivity",
            "e": -1,
            "phase": "fluid"
          }
        ]
      ],
      "reference": "L is the characteristic length of the declared geometry and k_f is the fluid conductivity. State whether h and Nu are local or mean values.",
      "source": "spec-10"
    },
    {
